  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126069,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Single lesions typically occur on the face, and multiple lesions favour the face and neck.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:29:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126070,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours of the follicular infundibulum occur as solitary or (more often) multiple smooth or slightly hyperkeratotic and hypopigmented papules arranged in plaques {2069339; 7593824; 8786188}. Multiple lesions are more common on photoexposed areas and appear as grouped hypopigmented macules with a reticulated pattern, or they may present as lesions mimicking hypopigmented plane warts {19389540; 20137756; 24685851; 26143173}. In some patients, eruptive lesions have been described {6824362; 8786188; 29693061}. Tumour of the follicular infundibulum may develop in a pre-existing naevus sebaceus of Jadassohn {9082365; 19652586; 25761672}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:29:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126071,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 138,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The relative frequency reported is 3&ndash;17&nbsp;cases per 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;skin biopsies {19633534} or 12&nbsp;cases per 121&nbsp;500&nbsp;biopsies {7490369}. There is no sex predilection {19633534}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:29:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
